  "title": "Erdős Problem #80",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $c>0$ and let $f_c(n)$ be the maximal $m$ such that every graph $G$ with $n$ vertices and at least $cn^2$ edges, where each edge is contained in at least one triangle, must contain a book of size $m$, that is, an edge shared by at least $m$ different triangles.\nEstimate $f_c(n)$. In particular, is it true that $f_c(n)>n^{\\epsilon}$ for some $\\epsilon>0$? Or $f_c(n)\\gg \\log n$?",
